From: Austin Schuh <austin.schuh@bluerivertech.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gen_config_m4: emit `.type sym,%function` on ARM ELF

On ARM, the GNU assembler treats `@` as the line-comment character, so
the default ELF spelling `.type sym,@function` is silently truncated to
`.type sym,` and gas fails with:

    Error: unrecognized symbol type ""

GNU `as` on ARM also accepts the equivalent `%function` (and `#function`)
spellings; autoconf-built gmp picks one of those at configure time via
`GMP_ASM_TYPE`. gen_config_m4 currently hard-codes the ELF default
unconditionally, so override it for ARM ELF targets.

This matches the equivalent `acinclude.m4:GMP_ASM_TYPE` behavior in
upstream gmp.
---
 bazel/gen_config_m4.cc | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bazel/gen_config_m4.cc b/bazel/gen_config_m4.cc
--- a/bazel/gen_config_m4.cc
+++ b/bazel/gen_config_m4.cc
@@ -223,7 +223,13 @@
     out << "define(<GLOBL_ATTR>, <" << syntax->globl_attr << ">)\n";
     out << "define(<GSYM_PREFIX>, <" << syntax->gsym_prefix << ">)\n";
     out << "define(<RODATA>, <" << rodata << ">)\n";
-    out << "define(<TYPE>, <" << syntax->type_fmt << ">)\n";
+    // ARM uses `@` as the line-comment character, so the ELF default
+    // `.type sym,@function` is misparsed by gas as `.type sym,` followed by a
+    // comment. Use `%function` (also accepted by gas on ARM) instead.
+    if (is_arm(arch) && syntax == &ELF_SYNTAX)
+        out << "define(<TYPE>, <.type\t$1,%$2>)\n";
+    else
+        out << "define(<TYPE>, <" << syntax->type_fmt << ">)\n";
     out << "define(<SIZE>, <" << syntax->size_fmt << ">)\n";
     out << "define(<LSYM_PREFIX>, <" << syntax->lsym_prefix << ">)\n";
     out << "define(<W32>, <" << syntax->w32 << ">)\n";
